######## lab_10_07_analyze_probes.py ########

==============================================================================
10.07 30 seeds, SO-RSI, planted start, budget 8000
==============================================================================
anomaly     count/run  probes  blocker found  later resolved   typical meaning
recurrence       51.4     457             32              32   same category / same edit failing repeatedly -> look for the
opposing          2.6       0              0               0   an edit reverses a recently accepted one -> look for conflic
mismatch         25.8     269             42              42   edit accepted but its target did not improve -> the model of
LIMITATION: 'opposing' fires (2.6/run) but never launched a probe - the triggering edit is a removal and our counterfactual probe needs an additive edit to test. It is logged, not acted on.

why each probe addresses a ROOT cause:
  recurrence  stops thrashing: converts 'try another patch' into 'ask what blocks every patch'
  opposing    oscillation means two edits fight; the probe tests whether a third stage causes the fight
  mismatch    expectation violated while the loop believes it progressed (ties are accepted) - hidden failure made visible

blockers named across 30 runs: {'punct_stripper': 29, 'mixed_pattern_drops_whole': 16, 'frac_pattern_swapped': 12, 'range_pattern_lower_bound': 11, 'note_comma_greedy': 3, 'unit_alias_collision': 2, 'strip_first_item_word': 1}
status of investigations: {'inconclusive': 652, 'resolved': 74}
runs where the PLANTED blocker was named: 29/30; named AND its removal accepted: 29/30
EMERGENT blockers (created by the loop's own buggy variants, not planted): 45 investigations named one
probe cost: 2445 evals/run = 31% of budget; 24.2 probes/run
probes that came back inconclusive (no stage blocked the edit): 90%
persistent inquiry memory of seed 100 -> results/inquiry_memory_seed100.json


