==============================================================================
10.16 B. which environment when?  (claims = course summaries, unverified)
==============================================================================

RSIGym (EaaS)
   feature : training / inference / rollout / eval / sandbox as reusable services, shared budget + permissions, data/harness/joint tracks
   choose when: you must compare MANY RSI methods fairly on cost; you need budget + permission control
   limit   : heavy: needs real services; overkill for a single toy loop

Terminal-RSI
   feature : terminal-agent infrastructure with RL (actor/critic phases)
   choose when: the object improved is a terminal agent trained with RL
   limit   : needs RL infra; not laptop-reproducible (course marks it analysis-only)

R2Orch
   feature : self-play environment: inner loop improves an orchestrator, outer loop improves the improver
   choose when: the thing improved is a multi-agent orchestrator and you can generate tasks
   limit   : task proposer can collapse to easy tasks unless rewarded for diverse outcomes

This repo's testbed
   feature : one scaffold (parser source) + exact-match data + a Meter; edits are real diffs, scores come from execution
   choose when: you want fully reproducible, laptop-scale evidence about SELECTION / DIAGNOSIS / HARNESS ideas
   limit   : proposer is a stub; single domain; planted structure; not evidence about LLM agents


